?p1 Which environment variable should be set to enable backtraces for errors only?
  = RUST_LIB_BACKTRACE=1
  > README.md:85 #e2e2fa1521f8
?p2 What does the backtrace! macro return when the std feature is not enabled?
  = None
  > src/backtrace.rs:17 #8da9f519eca1
?p3 What happens to the internal state of a Linked Chain when next_back() is called?
  = It collects all remaining errors into a Vec and transitions the state to Buffered.
  > src/chain.rs::DoubleEndedIterator.next_back #95c585d2e85c
?p4 Why does the implementation of context for Result use a match statement instead of map_err?
  = To save 2 useless frames off the captured backtrace.
